#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The code on this page was developed using the following requirements.\n"
"We recommend using these versions or newer.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kode di halaman ini dikembangkan menggunakan persyaratan berikut.\n"
"Kami menyarankan menggunakan versi ini atau yang lebih baru.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"In many situations – such as learning or debugging – it's helpful to visualize the state of a quantum computer. Here we assume you already have a particular state from simulation or state tomography.  It's only possible to view the states of small quantum systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
"Dalam banyak situasi — seperti saat belajar atau debugging — sangat membantu untuk memvisualisasikan state komputer kuantum. Di sini kita asumsikan kamu sudah memiliki state tertentu dari simulasi atau state tomography. Kita hanya bisa melihat state sistem kuantum yang kecil.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Using the output from functions\" type=\"tip\">\n"
"All functions on this page return rich objects. When the last line of a code cell outputs these objects, Jupyter notebooks display them below the cell. If you call these functions in some other environments or in scripts, you will need to explicitly show or save the outputs.\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Menggunakan output dari fungsi\" type=\"tip\">\n"
"Semua fungsi di halaman ini mengembalikan objek yang kaya. Ketika baris terakhir sel kode menghasilkan objek-objek ini, Jupyter notebooks akan menampilkannya di bawah sel. Jika kamu memanggil fungsi-fungsi ini di lingkungan lain atau dalam skrip, kamu perlu menampilkan atau menyimpan outputnya secara eksplisit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Most functions return images, which are `matplotlib.Figure` objects. Two options are:\n"
"- Call `.show()` on the returned object to open the image in a new window (assuming your configured matplotlib backend is interactive).\n"
"- Call `.savefig(\"out.png\")` to save the figure to `out.png` in the current working directory. The `savefig()` method takes a path so you can adjust the location and filename where you're saving the output. For example, `plot_state_city(psi).savefig(\"out.png\")`.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sebagian besar fungsi mengembalikan gambar, yaitu objek `matplotlib.Figure`. Dua opsi yang tersedia:\n"
"- Panggil `.show()` pada objek yang dikembalikan untuk membuka gambar di jendela baru (dengan asumsi backend matplotlib yang dikonfigurasi bersifat interaktif).\n"
"- Panggil `.savefig(\"out.png\")` untuk menyimpan gambar ke `out.png` di direktori kerja saat ini. Metode `savefig()` menerima path sehingga kamu bisa menyesuaikan lokasi dan nama file tempat menyimpan output. Misalnya, `plot_state_city(psi).savefig(\"out.png\")`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The LaTeX outputs are `IPython.display.Latex` objects. The best option in a non-Jupyter environment is to avoid this output by either printing the state for a text representation, or switching to the `latex_source` drawer to return a LaTeX source string.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"Output LaTeX adalah objek `IPython.display.Latex`. Opsi terbaik di lingkungan non-Jupyter adalah menghindari output ini dengan cara mencetak state untuk representasi teks, atau beralih ke drawer `latex_source` untuk mengembalikan string sumber LaTeX.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A quantum state is either a density matrix $\\rho$ (Hermitian matrix) or statevector $|\\psi\\rangle$ (complex vector). The density matrix is related to the statevector by\n"
msgstr "State kuantum bisa berupa matriks densitas $\\rho$ (matriks Hermitian) atau statevector $|\\psi\\rangle$ (vektor kompleks). Matriks densitas berkaitan dengan statevector melalui\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\rho = |\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|,$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\rho = |\\psi\\rangle\\langle \\psi|,$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "and is more general, as it can represent mixed states (positive sum of statevectors)\n"
msgstr "dan lebih umum karena bisa merepresentasikan mixed states (jumlah positif statevector)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\\rho = \\sum_k p_k |\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k |.$$\n"
msgstr "$$\\rho = \\sum_k p_k |\\psi_k\\rangle\\langle \\psi_k |.$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Qiskit represents quantum states through the `Statevector` and `DensityMatrix` classes and provides many visualization functions. See the sections after the following the code cell to see how Qiskit's different visualization functions plot the following quantum state.\n"
msgstr "Qiskit merepresentasikan state kuantum melalui kelas `Statevector` dan `DensityMatrix` serta menyediakan banyak fungsi visualisasi. Lihat bagian-bagian setelah sel kode berikut untuk melihat bagaimana berbagai fungsi visualisasi Qiskit memplot state kuantum berikut ini.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"LaTeX\" label=\"LaTeX\">\n"
"  While not technically a \"plot\", Qiskit can render LaTeX representations of both `Statevector` and `DensityMatrix` objects that display nicely in Jupyter notebooks. These follow the standard mathematical conventions for writing down quantum states. Read more in [Basics of quantum information: Single systems](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction).\n"
msgstr ""
"<Tabs>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"LaTeX\" label=\"LaTeX\">\n"
"  Meski secara teknis bukan \"plot\", Qiskit bisa merender representasi LaTeX dari objek `Statevector` maupun `DensityMatrix` yang tampil dengan baik di Jupyter notebooks. Representasi ini mengikuti konvensi matematika standar untuk menuliskan state kuantum. Baca lebih lanjut di [Dasar-dasar informasi kuantum: Sistem tunggal](/learning/courses/basics-of-quantum-information/single-systems/introduction).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Statevectors default to \"ket notation\", whereas density matrices are displayed as a 2×2 matrix.\n"
msgstr "  Statevector menggunakan \"notasi ket\" secara default, sedangkan matriks densitas ditampilkan sebagai matriks 2×2.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  You can also replace `\"latex\"` with `\"latex_source\"` to get the raw LaTeX string.\n"
msgstr "  Kamu juga bisa mengganti `\"latex\"` dengan `\"latex_source\"` untuk mendapatkan string LaTeX mentah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"City\" label=\"City\">\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"City\" label=\"City\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This plot displays the real and imaginary parts of each density matrix element in two three-dimensional bar charts.  It's called a \"city\" plot because the bars resemble skyscrapers in a city. The state we're plotting has the following density matrix.\n"
msgstr "  Plot ini menampilkan bagian real dan imajiner dari setiap elemen matriks densitas dalam dua diagram batang tiga dimensi. Disebut plot \"city\" karena batang-batangnya menyerupai gedung pencakar langit di sebuah kota. State yang kita plot memiliki matriks densitas berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 & \\frac{i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  - \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4} & - \\frac{i}{4} & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  + i\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  - \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4} & - \\frac{i}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 & \\frac{i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  - \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4} & - \\frac{i}{4} & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4} & \\frac{1}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  + i\n"
"  \\begin{bmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{i}{4}  \\\\\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0  \\\\\n"
"  - \\frac{\\sqrt{2} i}{4} & - \\frac{i}{4} & 0 & 0 \\\\\n"
"  \\end{bmatrix}\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_city) for more information.\n"
msgstr "  Lihat [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_city) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Hinton\" label=\"Hinton\">\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Hinton\" label=\"Hinton\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  This plot is very similar to the \"city\" plot, but the magnitude of each element is represented by the size of a square rather than the height of a bar. White squares represent elements with positive values, and black squares represent elements with negative values. The state we're plotting has the following density matrix.\n"
msgstr "  Plot ini sangat mirip dengan plot \"city\", namun besarnya setiap elemen direpresentasikan oleh ukuran kotak, bukan tinggi batang. Kotak putih mewakili elemen dengan nilai positif, dan kotak hitam mewakili elemen dengan nilai negatif. State yang kita plot memiliki matriks densitas berikut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_hinton) for more information.\n"
msgstr "  Lihat [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_hinton) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Pauli vector\" label=\"Pauli vector\">\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Pauli vector\" label=\"Vektor Pauli\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  An observable is a way of measuring a quantum state such that the possible measurement outcomes are real numbers. The expected value of the outcome is also known as the expectation value of the observable on that state, and it can be thought of as the average of infinitely many observations of that state.\n"
msgstr "  Observable adalah cara mengukur state kuantum sedemikian rupa sehingga hasil pengukuran yang mungkin adalah bilangan real. Nilai yang diharapkan dari hasil tersebut juga dikenal sebagai nilai ekspektasi observable pada state itu, dan bisa dianggap sebagai rata-rata dari pengamatan tak terbatas terhadap state tersebut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  Tensor products of Pauli matrices are all observables that return +1 or -1. This plot displays the expectation values of the state on different Pauli operators as a bar chart. All density matrices can be written as a sum of these Pauli matrices, weighted by their expectation values.\n"
msgstr "  Produk tensor dari matriks Pauli semuanya merupakan observable yang menghasilkan +1 atau -1. Plot ini menampilkan nilai ekspektasi state pada berbagai operator Pauli sebagai diagram batang. Semua matriks densitas bisa ditulis sebagai jumlah matriks Pauli ini, dikalikan bobotnya masing-masing berdasarkan nilai ekspektasinya.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  For example, this state can be written as the sum of terms:\n"
msgstr "  Sebagai contoh, state ini bisa ditulis sebagai jumlah dari suku-suku:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  $$\n"
"  |\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\tfrac{1}{4}II\n"
"  + \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}IX\n"
"  - \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}XY\n"
"  - \\tfrac{1}{8}YI\n"
"  - \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}YX\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}YZ\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}ZI\n"
"  + \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}ZX\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}ZZ\n"
"  $$\n"
msgstr ""
"  $$\n"
"  |\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi|\n"
"  =\n"
"  \\tfrac{1}{4}II\n"
"  + \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}IX\n"
"  - \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}XY\n"
"  - \\tfrac{1}{8}YI\n"
"  - \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}YX\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}YZ\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}ZI\n"
"  + \\tfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}ZX\n"
"  + \\tfrac{1}{8}ZZ\n"
"  $$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  You can also calculate these coefficients using `SparsePauliOp`.\n"
msgstr "  Kamu juga bisa menghitung koefisien-koefisien ini menggunakan `SparsePauliOp`.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_paulivec) for more information.\n"
msgstr "  Lihat [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_paulivec) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Qsphere\" label=\"Qsphere\">\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Qsphere\" label=\"Qsphere\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The \"QSphere\" is a Qiskit-unique view of a quantum state in which the amplitude and phase of each element in a statevector is plotted on the surface of a sphere. The thickness of each dot represents the amplitude, and the color represents the phase. For mixed states it will show a sphere for each component.\n"
msgstr "  \"QSphere\" adalah tampilan state kuantum unik dari Qiskit di mana amplitudo dan fase dari setiap elemen dalam statevector diplot pada permukaan bola. Ketebalan setiap titik merepresentasikan amplitudo, dan warnanya merepresentasikan fase. Untuk mixed states, akan ditampilkan bola untuk setiap komponen.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_qsphere) for more information.\n"
msgstr "  Lihat [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_state_qsphere) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Bloch\" label=\"Bloch\">\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"<TabItem value=\"Bloch\" label=\"Bloch\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The Bloch vector of a qubit state is its expectation value in the X, Y, and Z Pauli observables mapped to the X, Y, and Z axes in three-dimensional space. This plot projects multi-qubit quantum states onto the single-qubit space and plots each qubit on a Bloch sphere. This visualization only shows the expectation values of individual qubits. It can't show correlations between qubits and so can't fully describe entangled quantum states.\n"
msgstr "  Vektor Bloch dari state qubit adalah nilai ekspektasinya dalam observable Pauli X, Y, dan Z yang dipetakan ke sumbu X, Y, dan Z dalam ruang tiga dimensi. Plot ini memproyeksikan state kuantum multi-Qubit ke ruang qubit tunggal dan memplot setiap qubit pada bola Bloch. Visualisasi ini hanya menampilkan nilai ekspektasi dari qubit individual. Plot ini tidak bisa menunjukkan korelasi antar qubit sehingga tidak bisa sepenuhnya mendeskripsikan state kuantum yang terjalin (entangled).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  See the [API documentation](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_bloch_multivector) for more information.\n"
msgstr "  Lihat [dokumentasi API](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.visualization.plot_bloch_multivector) untuk informasi lebih lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"
msgstr ""
"</TabItem>\n"
"</Tabs>\n"

